# Command-line interface contract

- `dpi_detector.py` is the repository-level launch entry point; `cli` owns console interaction and test-run orchestration, because interface concerns must remain separate from scanning behavior.
- Scanner behavior lives in `core`, and shared configuration, file, network, and error-classification support lives in `utils`, because those areas have separate ownership contracts.
- User-visible flags and invocation examples are documented in `README.md`; keep that documentation aligned when the interface changes, because it is the public usage reference.

